From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: shphadnis <134159681+shphadnis@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 9 Nov 2026 19:55:36 -0800
Subject: [PATCH] spectro: sync vsphere-copy-offload-populator vendoring with
 CDI v1.66.1

Patch 0019 bumped kubevirt.io/containerized-data-importer-api to v1.66.1
in the root module but left the nested vsphere-copy-offload-populator
module on v1.63.1. That module resolves forklift through
`replace => ../../`, so Go selects v1.66.1 (and testify v1.11.1 with it).
The image build runs `go mod download`, which rewrites go.mod to those
versions, and the vendored build then fails:

  go: inconsistent vendoring in .../cmd/vsphere-copy-offload-populator:
    kubevirt.io/containerized-data-importer-api@v1.66.1: is explicitly
    required in go.mod, but not marked as explicit in vendor/modules.txt

This broke build-vsphere-copy-offload-populator-image in the
4.10.9-rc.1 pack build. Run `go mod tidy && go mod vendor` in the
module: go.mod moves to CDI API v1.66.1 and testify v1.11.1, and vendor/
is regenerated, which also refreshes the vendored copy of the root
forklift API from ../../.

Resolves: None

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
